Engine: the turn-time popups — their own ids and what they show, "TPOP" (open fix 49).

STATUS: APPLIED 29 September 2026 by work order 188 (Part 4, the
turn-change messages in HD), under the order's advance approval of the
engine fixes a part needs ("Engine fixes: approved in advance for this
run") — orion2re 6859e163 on orionlayer-local (before: 76f8c438), this
file's diff byte for byte (index lines included). Required by
tools/version_check.py since work order 188.

PROOF ON THE TIP IT WAS APPLIED TO (work order 188): in a scratch clone of
orionlayer-local at 76f8c438 this file applied with `patch -p1 --dry-run`
and `patch -p1`, no offset, no fuzz, the applied tree's diff equal to it;
the six changed .cpp compiled alone with the build's own command
(-fsyntax-only), exit 0; six controls were refused by the compiler, exit 1
each — `g_turn_popup.kind` misspelt in ext_api.cpp and `ext::TurnPopupGuard`
misspelt `ext::TurnPopupGard` in turnsum.cpp, mainpups.cpp, science.cpp,
events.cpp and colland.cpp. Then applied to ~/orion2re (no offset), built
(ninja, no error) and committed.

To revert, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch: `git revert
6859e163` or `patch -R -p1`; then rebuild. See the entry,
doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md 49.

WIRE LAYOUT — "TPOP", written LAST (after MSGB), on any screen while a popup
is up. int16 little-endian. 'T''P''O''P', uint8 version 1, uint8 kind
(1 science, 2 turn summary, 3 leader for hire, 4 planet choice, 5 new
system, 6 leader level, 7 GNN, 8 combat target, 9 colony landing), int16
n_args, n_args x int16, title (int16 length + raw bytes), text (int16
length + raw bytes); kind 2 then int16 N and per message: int16 length +
bytes (MSG_::sprintf_msg_), uint8 jumps, int16 colony, uint8 page, int16
first field, uint8 field count; kinds 4, 5, 8 then int16 star, int16 grid
field, 5 x (int16 planet field, int16 planet), 15 x (int16 ship field,
int16 ship); kind 8 then 5 x int16 colony targets, int16 their count,
15 x int16 player targets, int16 their count. The arguments per kind and
every popup's fields: doc/brief_turn_messages.md and core/turnpopup.py.

WHAT IT IS FOR
At turn change the report phase runs its popups under SCREEN_MAIN
(Reports_Screen_ sets it, mainscr2.cpp:118) and the Turn Summary drops its
own 40 after one tick (turnsum.cpp:90), so a client cannot tell a leader
offer, a planet choice or a discovery from the galaxy map; and what each
shows — the science room's discoveries, the Turn Summary's lines, the GNN's
news, the planet choice's star and planets — is on no wire. One guard per
popup reports a synthetic id (59 leader for hire, 60 planet choice, 61 new
system, 62 a leader's level, 63 GNN, 64 combat target; 40 kept for the whole
Turn Summary; 52 and 33 keep theirs) and holds the popup's content, sent as
block "TPOP" after MSGB: its kind, its arguments (ids, star, leader, cost,
the live answer fields), its title and text as the game formatted them, and
per kind a tail (the Turn Summary's rendered lines with their jump flags; the
system display's field-to-planet map; the combat targets). Nothing the game
reads is changed.

